[{"id":"VRCE-6-79-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":1,"english":"Having in the conflict slain that conqueror of enemies, Lakşmaņa graced with auspicious marks, with his body bathed in blood, experienced delight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.619,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"37e09046ded28f717491d248a534ddf339b3b04c7f1d72d5ca2c38e26c148d41","compact":"755eead02970f4ba888f3585a1bc21dfaa2beeda76e7d5e73ecd6f747c6f782a","nasal":"2eeb19af62ffb841d0f0a0d9c17232d6a3682c8f1e044faec9f3ec7737f9b834"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":2,"english":"Then supporting himself on Vibhīşana and Hanuman, the exceedingly powerful Lakşmaņa endowed with prowess, taking Jambavan, Hanuman and all the monkeys with him, speedily went to the place where Sugrīva and Raghava were.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3b0c7dd45ad2befb07f30af3f561b20b9eda768554b88aeadad48ad024276e10","compact":"9951c62b4145303831698c0b49a5fb466c5c8afc962c4f56c15f854e7b92bbfa","nasal":"dce5a81787024e6a771ad7d80a78aa2f1961f7175720edf0395dd226d7581e5b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":3,"english":"Then supporting himself on Vibhīşana and Hanuman, the exceedingly powerful Lakşmaņa endowed with prowess, taking Jambavan, Hanuman and all the monkeys with him, speedily went to the place where Sugrīva and Raghava were.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5ca6f543ac0e22a2105b564be6a428dfc026dfb9a72f63232007c1107f23bcc4","compact":"ffc7cea0d04b5f7485e97a4a1a0dfde882b292cbb169e9fc02e6a1771d34b1b0","nasal":"94fdeb9057bc16788d34cfd3f5c6ff55e3bef6803c0c636fe63ece27a530084b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":4,"english":"Then going round Rāma and saluted him, Sumitra's son stood before his brother, like Indra's brother staying before Sakra. And approaching with a look which of itself was significant,* the heroic Vibhīşaņa described to the high-souled Räghava the dreadful destruction of Indrajit. *i.e. of the destruction of Indrajit.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.67,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-3","DUTT-6-91-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7935b59941450288234b69bc8b6d27906f89eff2937f613b52ac2a0d1d41f2ba","compact":"d6654a9d354713e62812e8473a0448993eda1cba395ba0a677833586516bbf2e","nasal":"284ea763d42c7ce56e2897415f81f939189a3f13afffa90d8836f4372ec82b31"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":5,"english":"Then the delighted Vibhişaņa related to Rāma how the high-souled Lakşmaņa had cut off the head of Ravana's son.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.793,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"03a33fe6897cf069f0e7c99c95e0b7ac0fbf85ae10a6da2168df8aa2710589c9","compact":"d307a63ada8ab6c5543eef97223b545b8c440ffd3d901788cbda35537ab1b0b9","nasal":"b4531ec7e2e20e3d02924e97403a1888714d0323e4f81a8016644c28ae3eccb0"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":6,"english":"Then smelling the head of the bashful Laks miana, enhancer of fame, (Rāma) endowed with prowess, from affection forcibly hugged him into his lap. And making him seat on his lap, and overpowering him with embraces,* (Rama) again and again tenderly eyed his brother, Lakş imana. * Aapiritam-fac) pained. Rāmānaya says this epithet refers to Laksmana's having been wounded in the encounter. I differ from him. And moved with grief, that best of persons, Rama, smelling head of Laksmana, wounded with darts and having his person pierced (with salms, sighing and breathing hard-and nursing ms body with his hand, addressed Laksmana, soothing him.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.567,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-8","DUTT-6-91-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5804e49be28f954db9d287de1d5b2f533deecbf7e4192cb35bfa7423de67f2da","compact":"a9a8386261843f86e8866b63a112620f3b1a8b970c552becd82f04e4c03c7e38","nasal":"ccd37507d1dbca9add37b0833cbbaa3fd5e9f93e6efee24ebececcb49d81494a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":7,"english":"Rāvana will for certain sally out, hearing his son brought down. That unconquerable lord of Rakşasas, aggrieved for the destruction of his son, marching out, shall I slay, environed with a mighty force.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.541,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"58642f5e650098a671a06b0318d0a8e75cf8f2c400349580d51b42a1c2ab01a2","compact":"7819cfcd570a1c7439441710f1773857658434c741a4f00dfe7a16d74055df83","nasal":"7819cfcd570a1c7439441710f1773857658434c741a4f00dfe7a16d74055df83"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":8,"english":"Rāvana will for certain sally out, hearing his son brought down. That unconquerable lord of Rakşasas, aggrieved for the destruction of his son, marching out, shall I slay, environed with a mighty force.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a3583ff5636dcf7f7806be3ade3534f7936ecc02e3307db0d23b33e803ae96ef","compact":"4fa3b4fda4cb8fd7ddbf0ba1c9b744777bbc7e346792ba7526d20305d3271902","nasal":"9f0d93d92b7e502dddc01a72844e8372b4f48fa0847fb05d8b62b746700a6dd9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":9,"english":"O Lakşmaņa, the conqueror of Sakra having in battle been slain by you-who are my lord-Sītā and the entire) earth are not incapable of being obtained by me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.793,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8c4e8f90d2718370e173974f8a71b7d4210ab200e88703d7df4c5529ccb2ef86","compact":"887980ff0a00110e9ce5a66abe34aca981616ce95d11f980656923c68aab7867","nasal":"887980ff0a00110e9ce5a66abe34aca981616ce95d11f980656923c68aab7867"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":10,"english":"Having thus soothed and embraced his brother, Raghu's son Rama highly rejoiced calling Suşeņa said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"70e367d63efe3b5696ad0a2b1f9cae4bee34225f7067f1508b63043f0c25db3e","compact":"a944ef18e70837a61a1aa127df45a97ed2b17c1d00b24c39989776407a289275","nasal":"a944ef18e70837a61