tent medicine to the nose of Laksmana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"51c6b2265e68b37b1c9362ac1bccfba7ed3cb0cd7f368edb36f59699fb8950e6","compact":"d16d3fb289e0b527e0460046679fd23985e793a268aa91dfacdd2a0e33a142df","nasal":"d16d3fb289e0b527e0460046679fd23985e793a268aa91dfacdd2a0e33a142df"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":14,"english":"And smelling the same, he got healed; he was relieved of his pain and his outgoing vitality was shut up.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.824,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"952db76dbf6e741595d71cd149001bd33bcf1ffcf4fd24dd8dda65a09495695a","compact":"473a973bae15276aed2ef82b9c5c5469f3351c6bebf86c43a2b9afb654b085bb","nasal":"f83bc345f8064ee07d9ad178f93746dea4762e848c15cba17479add8f4b18e59"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":15,"english":"At the mandate of Rāghava he likewise treated his friends headed by Vibhișaņa and all the principal monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dd8cc517e59a9e5b4904a3bf259def8535d74aeb6709126a3f6962fb97973cb6","compact":"2da3a6e6c5d14b435ea711cda594faf0c4fc9efbaea7474178496a159ed6a45e","nasal":"2da3a6e6c5d14b435ea711cda594faf0c4fc9efbaea7474178496a159ed6a45e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":16,"english":"And restored to his natural condition, Sumitrā's son, healed, and with his exhaustion removed, and his suffering gone off in a moment, experienced exhilaration of spirits.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.426,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"04fa99ffa1126535059c6ee1f80d61fae9776db543c1fa67302aee54c11279a1","compact":"999ddca2b305dcdcde93a780c7f5e16a2659b3501c6bc3d2cb22303e08c48ab5","nasal":"8462ccb61a4fe56b8e25037f3e3425e491161a1aaa606ce871d5c53a21194d85"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":17,"english":"Rāma and the monkey-king and Vibhīşaņa! and the powerful lord of bears along with their hosts, seeing Sumitrā's son risen hale, rejoiced greatly in delight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.639,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9876c4ebf7e3d713031a8aaf05240f622180396a2aba861a8fae9655aa49a181","compact":"05c5d12eb26678b8edab80bc5ee517c44059d1f2df93029bce51777368de1127","nasal":"edf3ec56d8b1cb3092ec6e1aa4b055c24a7ec9b2e23438dfac3c694610e652cc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-79-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":79,"verse":18,"english":"The high-souled son of Dasaratha honoured exceedingly that exceedingly hard feat of Laks amana; and the monkey-king, hearing that the conqueror of Sakra had fallen in fight, was filled with joy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.62,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-91-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6079018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c9873ccf9417d03b6ed14a2fbff13704af514d5d1043ff84daf460e713021bd3","compact":"4c204dd862346e4614df593001